  "description": "Recent photographed sightings in Sweden from GBIF (many from iNaturalist): the photos as a grid, which classes of life they show and who took them. Statistics: a count of sightings is not abundance, it follows observer effort. Bird records per province are divided by all photographed records there (the exposure) into a share with a 95% interval; the big provinces lead in counts, not in share. Caveats: a share is still not abundance, and GBIF's province names mix counties and historical provinces.",
